※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4485

※ What picking answers with is however many were picked, held in room enough for
※ all of them -- and room enough for all of them is what the shape says.  Where
※ the type does not say it, the room would have to be taken while the program
※ runs, which is an allocation and a change to something that outlives the call.

fn picked(xs: u8⟦⟧, want: bool⟦4⟧) → u8:
    let got: u8⟦⟧ = xs⟦want⟧
    got⟦0⟧

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    let v: u8⟦4⟧ = ⟦1u8, 2u8, 3u8, 4u8⟧
    picked(v, ⟦true, false, false, false⟧)
